(A loop body runs only on some paths, like a branch: a list declared in it
 under a parameter's name lasts as long as the body, and after the loop the
 name is the parameter again.)
To 'loop' with a list called items.
    a number called n is 0.
    While n is less than 2, a list called items is ["local"], append "y" to items, Set n to n add 1.
    append "x" to items.
    Print "inside: {items}".

a list called xs is ["old"].
'loop' of xs.
Print "xs: {xs}".
